    "progressSummary": "PROVED: Created ArithmeticSeriesOQ02OQ04OQ01.lean with 11 theorems (0 sorries, 0 axioms). Main result: C(n,k) * k! = descFactorial(n,k) (ordered selection formula). Dual to ascending: C(n+k,k) * k! = ascFactorial(n+1,k). Key Mathlib lemma: Nat.descFactorial_eq_factorial_mul_choose.",
    "builtItems": [
      "choose_descFactorial: C(n,k) * k! = descFactorial(n,k)",
      "choose_product: C(n,k) * k! = ∏ i in range k, (n-i)",
      "choose_full_factorial: C(n,k) * k! * (n-k)! = n!",
      "factorial_dvd_descFactorial: k! | descFactorial(n,k)",
      "ascending_descending_duality: connects ascending and descending factorial identities",
      "Specializations: k=1,2,3 and concrete checks"
    ],
    "insights": [
      "Key Mathlib lemma: Nat.descFactorial_eq_factorial_mul_choose states n.descFactorial k = k! * n.choose k",
      "Key Mathlib lemma: Nat.descFactorial_eq_prod_range states n.descFactorial k = ∏ i in range k, (n-i)",
      "Dual pair: descending uses C(n,k), ascending uses C(n+k,k) as simplicial numbers",
      "Nat.descFactorial_self: n.descFactorial n = n! (boundary case)",
      "Nat.factorial_mul_descFactorial: (n-k)! * descFactorial(n,k) = n! (structural property)"
